━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ ThemeScope is Tuple

+ made TypeId
+ sheet TypeId
+ statement SyntaxId
+ number U32

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Styles is facet of Checker
    sees Comprehensions
    sees LiveActions
    sees Markup

_ theme-statement SyntaxId = 0
_ theme-number U32 = U32.max
_ style-mark U32 = 0
_ collecting Bool = false
_ framed U32 = 0

────────────────────
_ do revise-application
    - index U32

` Counts a change to an application of a style rule that another pass cannot take in with the
` instance changing it: one another instance recorded. The merge takes in the instance's own as
` they end, with the state cells and the values of rules they name (`Facts.absorb-applications`).
if facts.style-applications[index].instance != instance
    facts.revised += 1

────────────────────
+ do check-gate-test
    - condition SyntaxId

` The function that tests again the condition a style rule written on a markup element is
` applied under, as the reference's gate evaluates it in its live action: the condition typed
` again as the body of a closure that answers whether it holds, which must be a `Bool`.
prepare()
instances.set-returns(instance, types.bool-type, types.bool-type, .return-declared)
if infer(condition) != types.bool-type
    decline(condition)
finish-errors(frame)
close()

────────────────────
+ do style-again Bool
    - statement SyntaxId
    - rhs SyntaxId
    - row StyleDeclaration

` Types the value of a style declaration a live action makes again, as where it is written.
. property = facts.style-properties[row.property]
. written = style-value(rhs, property.type)
if written == invalid-type || written == no-type
    = false
= conversions.convert(statement, rhs, written, property.type, .reason-assignment) != invalid-type

────────────────────
+ do demand-styles
    - receiver TypeId
    - site SyntaxId

` Registers the styles a class being made uses, and those the classes above it use, base
` first, as the reference does as it compiles a constructor: each style is numbered as it is
` first used, and its registration placed at the declaration of the constructor. No two styles
` a class sees may name one property. Then the classes' defaults are applied
` (`apply-style-defaults`). A using of a style sheet has no shape here, nor has one that is
` wrong in a class of another module, nor a property of an optional of a type that queries the
` markup the object is in.
if receiver == no-type || receiver == invalid-type || types.intrinsic-of(receiver) != .class
    =
. chain [TypeId]
. level TypeId? = receiver
while level && types.intrinsic-of(level) == .class
    chain += level
    level = types.base-of(level)
. visible [TypeId]
for position in 0 .. < chain.length
    for ref in sheet-parts(class-ref(types, chain[chain.length - 1 - position]))
        . owner = program.modules[ref.module]
        for member in owner.member-pool[part-members(ref)]
            do match? owner.decls[member]
                | .decl-property(property)
                    if property.type-syntax != 0 && queries-markup(ref, property.type-syntax) && query-type(ref, property.type-syntax) == no-type
                        decline(site)
                        =
                | .decl-using(using)
                    if using-sheet(ref, using) != no-type
                        continue
                    . used = using-style(ref, using, site)
                    if used == no-type
                        =
                    . index = style-index(used, site, true)
                    if index == U32.max
                        =
                    if visible.find(used) == null
                        if !distinct-style(index, visible, ref.module, using.syntax, site)
                            =
                        visible += used
if program.module-by-name("core/style")
    apply-style-defaults(chain, site)

────────────────────
_ do apply-style-defaults
    - chain [TypeId]
    - site SyntaxId

` The defaults of the classes of an object being made, base first, as the reference applies
` them once a constructor's body and the rules of each class have run: the rule `• This` each
` class writes declares at the defaults layer, each class's at a site of its own, its orders
` from a band of its own (`style-defaults-band`), the states its `when`s name the class's
` (`gate-when`). A line whose value reads something tracked is declared again by the action
` the object's class makes, as at an element. A rule `• This` that applies rules after its name
` applies them as an element's would (`apply-rule`), at the defaults layer, under the style
` sheets of the markup that made the object, as the reference's constructor applies them. Then
` come the rules and style lines of the class's root `<This` (`apply-root-rules`), and the rules
` of the style sheets the chain uses that the class's name answers (`apply-themed-defaults`). Each
` application of the defaults is marked `made` by its class. A rule `• This` written in another
` module is applied in that module (`enter-module`). A rule `• This` that takes values is
` declined.
for position in 0 .. < chain.length
    . level = chain[chain.length - 1 - position]
    . order = (position as U32) * style-defaults-band
    . ref = class-ref(types, level)
    . owner = program.modules[ref.module]
    do match? owner.decls[ref.decl]
        | .decl-class(class)
            for member in owner.member-pool[class.members]
                do match? owner.decls[member]
                    | .decl-style-rule(rule)
                        . applying = this-rule && owner.tree.applies-rules(rule.syntax)
                            .. this-rule = rule.name.text == "This"
                        if rule.name.text == "This" && !owner.tree.rule-takes-nothing(rule.syntax)
                            decline(site)
                            =
                        if rule.name.text == "This"
                            . unit = instances.intern-initializer(ref.module, member, level)
                            if instances.rows[unit].state == .instance-in-progress
                                decline(site)
                                =
                            demand-body(unit)
                            panics.note-inlined(instance, unit)
                            if !note-style-errors(unit, site)
                                =
                            if applying
                                . home = enter-module(ref.module)
                                . next = apply-defaults-rules
                                    - rule.syntax
                                    - level
                                    - chain[0]
                                    - unit
                                    - order
                                enter-module(home)
                                if next == U32.max
                                    =
                                if next != order
                                    facts.style-sites += StyleSite
                                        - instance
                                        - ref.module
                                        - rule.syntax
                                order = next
                                continue
                            . ungated [StyleWhen]
                            for branch in owner.tree.rule-whens(owner.tree.rule-body(rule.syntax))
                                if !gate-when(site, level, ref.module, branch, ungated)
                                    =
                            . count = facts.style-declaration-count(unit)
                            if count != 0 || facts.updates-properties(unit)
                                facts.style-applications += StyleApplication
                                    - instance
                                    - ref.module
                                    - rule.syntax
                                    - unit
                                    - 0
                                    - order
                                facts.style-applications[facts.style-applications.length - 1].made = level
                                revise-application((facts.style-applications.length - 1) as U32)
                                if !bind-defaults-slots(site, level, unit, last-application)
                                    =
                                .. last-application = (facts.style-applications.length - 1) as U32
                                if facts.authors-in(unit)
                                    facts.style-applications[facts.style-applications.length - 1].action = demand-style-gates(chain[0])
                                    revise-application((facts.style-applications.length - 1) as U32)
                                if !choose-updater(latest-application, site, level)
                                    =
                                .. latest-application = (facts.style-applications.length - 1) as U32
                                share-defaults(facts.style-applications.length - 1, [unit], count)
                            if count != 0
                                facts.style-sites += StyleSite(instance, ref.module, rule.syntax)
                                order += count
    order = apply-root-rules(level, ref, chain[0], order, site)
    if order == U32.max
        =
    if !apply-themed-defaults(level, chain[0], band-order, site)
        =
    .. band-order = (position as U32) * style-defaults-band + style-defaults-band / 2

────────────────────
_ do apply-themed-defaults Bool
    - level TypeId
    - made TypeId
    - order U32
    - site SyntaxId

` Applies the rules taking no values that the style sheets the chain of an object being made uses
` write by the name of its class `level`, among that class's defaults, as the reference's
` `styleThemeClass` finds them: those `sheet-rules` finds in the sheets of the chain and their
` variants, each as `apply-defaults-rules` applies a rule `• This`, in the module of the sheet
` that writes it, at a site of its own, from `order`, the upper half of the class's band, under
` the gates of the variants that write it (`gate-applications`). Where a class of the chain
` writes a rule of the name, an element applies that one instead, and none is applied here.
` Answers false where one is declined or reported.
. ref = class-ref(types, level)
. named = ""
. declared SyntaxId = 0
do match? program.modules[ref.module].decls[ref.decl]
    | .decl-class(class)
        named = class.name.text
        declared = class.syntax
. name = program.store-atom(named)
. (owner, written, writes) = class-style-rule(made, name)
=? true if owner != no-type
. none [TypeId]
. sheets [TypeId]
. members [DeclRef]
. gates [U64]
. entered = enter-module(ref.module)
. (status, found, missed) = sheet-rules(made, name, none, declared, sheets, members, gates, U32.max, false, true)
enter-module(entered)
if status == 1
    decline(site)
=? false if status != 0
. next = order
for position in 0 .. < sheets.length
    . member = members[position]
    . syntax SyntaxId = 0
    do match? program.modules[member.module].decls[member.decl]
        | .decl-style-rule(rule)
            syntax = rule.syntax
    . home = enter-module(member.module)
    . unit = rule-unit(sheets[position], member, level, syntax)
    if unit == no-instance
        enter-module(home)
        decline(site)
        = false
    if !note-style-errors(unit, site)
        enter-module(home)
        = false
    . first = facts.style-applications.length
    . applied = apply-defaults-rules(syntax, level, made, unit, next)
    . gated = ordered && gate-applications(first as U32, sheets[position], gates[position], syntax)
        .. ordered = applied != U32.max
    if gated && applied != next
        facts.style-sites += StyleSite(instance, member.module, syntax)
    enter-module(home)
    =? false if !gated
    next = applied
= true

────────────────────
_ do bind-defaults-slots Bool
    - site SyntaxId
    - level TypeId
    - unit InstanceId
    - application U32

. sheeted = markup-sheets.length
. context = instances.rows[instance].context
if context != U32.max
    . held = instances.contexts[context]
    for position in held.first + held.styles .. < held.first + held.styles + held.sheets
        markup-sheets += instances.context-types[position]
        sheet-levels += instances.context-levels[position]
. bound = bind-rule-slots(site, level, unit, application)
while markup-sheets.length > sheeted
    markup-sheets.pop()
    sheet-levels.pop()
= bound

────────────────────
_ do note-style-errors Bool
    - unit InstanceId
    - site SyntaxId

if facts.authors-in(unit)
    demand-errors(unit)
    if instances.signatures[unit].errors.count != 0 && !hands-off(unit)
        decline(site)
        = false
note-unit-errors(unit, site)
= true

────────────────────
_ do apply-defaults-rules U32
    - syntax SyntaxId
    - level TypeId
    - made TypeId
    - unit InstanceId
    - order U32

` Applies a rule `• This` that the class `level` of an object being made writes and applies
` rules, and the rules it applies, as an element's rules are applied (`apply-rule`) to an object
` of that class, as the reference resolves them, but at the defaults layer, seeing the style
` sheets of the markup that made the object, which the constructor is made for, before those of
` the class, and the rules written in its rules, as the root's are seen (`apply-root-rules`),
` generating no content. A declaration that reads something tracked is declared again
` by the action of the object's class. Answers the order the next takes, or `U32.max`.
. first = facts.style-applications.length
. context = instances.rows[instance].context
. sheeted = markup-sheets.length
. scoped = rule-scopes.length
if context != U32.max
    . held = instances.contexts[context]
    for position in held.first + held.styles .. < held.first + held.styles + held.sheets
        markup-sheets += instances.context-types[position]
        sheet-levels += instances.context-levels[position]
    for position in held.scope-first .. < held.scope-first + held.scopes
        if instances.context-cells[position] == 0 && instances.context-valued[position] == U32.max
            rule-scopes += ScopeUse(instances.context-scopes[position])
. active [InstanceId]
. applied [InstanceId]
. ungated [StyleWhen]
. generates = preparing
preparing = preparing.content-off = true
preparing = preparing.values-once = true
preparing = preparing.site = 0
. framing = framed
. next = apply-rule(syntax, level, unit, order, 0, U32.max, 0, ungated, active, applied)
preparing = generates
while markup-sheets.length > sheeted
    markup-sheets.pop()
    sheet-levels.pop()
while rule-scopes.length > scoped
    rule-scopes.pop()
if next != U32.max
    for index in first .. < facts.style-applications.length
        facts.style-applications[index].layer = 0
        revise-application(index as U32)
        if facts.style-applications[index].outer == U32.max
            facts.style-applications[index].made = level
            revise-application(index as U32)
        if facts.style-applications[index].action != no-instance
            facts.style-applications[index].action = demand-style-gates(made)
            revise-application(index as U32)
    if framed == framing
        share-defaults(first, applied, next - order)
= next

────────────────────
_ do share-defaults
    - first Size
    - applied [InstanceId]
    - count U32

=? if count == 0 || first >= facts.style-applications.length || !shares-rule(applied, count)
. last = facts.style-applications.length
for index in first .. < last
    . application = facts.style-applications[index]
    =? if application.cell != U32.max || outer-held
    .. outer-held = application.outer-cells != U32.max || application.around-values != U32.max
    =? if written-values || application.prepared || application.updater != no-instance
    .. written-values = application.written != 0 || application.values != no-instance
for index in first .. < last
    . unit = facts.style-applications[index].unit
    demand-errors(unit)
    =? if instances.signatures[unit].errors.count != 0
facts.style-applications[first].shared = true
revise-application(first as U32)
facts.style-applications[first].span = count
revise-application(first as U32)

────────────────────
_ do apply-root-rules U32
    - level TypeId
    - ref DeclRef
    - made TypeId
    - order U32
    - site SyntaxId

` Applies the style rules the root `<This` of the markup the class `level` of an object being
` made writes after `•`, as the reference's constructor applies them once the class's rule
` `• This` has (`compileRootThisStyleDefaults`): each as an element's would to an object of that
` class (`apply-written-rules`), seeing none the others bring into view, at the defaults layer,
` at one site of the root's, from an order, under the style sheets of the markup that made the
` object and the rules written in its rules that no `when` or rule taking values holds. The
` rules written in the rules they apply come into view in the class's content (`root-scopes`),
` not here, so no state cell is kept for them, and a rule here that applies one under such a cell
` is declined. The values an application gives are typed by an instance of their own for the
` class, under the constructor's context (`check-root-values`), and those the rules it applies
` give the rules they apply are evaluated once, as the reference's constructor evaluates them
` (`values-once`). Then each line of the root that names no property of the class declares a
` style there, typed as an instance of its own (`check-root-style`). Content the rules' lines
` generate is declined (`content-refused`). A root written in another module is applied in that
` module (`enter-module`). A declaration that reads something tracked is declared again by the
` action of the object's class `made`. Answers the order the next takes, or `U32.max`.
. owner = program.modules[ref.module]
. content SyntaxId = 0
. members = RowRange'DeclId()
do match? owner.decls[ref.decl]
    | .decl-class(class)
        content = class.content
        members = class.members
if content == 0
    = order
. root = owner.tree.root-this(content)
. applications = RowRange'SyntaxId()
. lines [DeclId]
do match? owner.tree.nodes[root]
    | .node-markup(row)
        applications = row.style-rule-applications
        do match? owner.tree.nodes[row.body]
            | .node-block(block)
                for statement in owner.tree.children[block.body]
                    do match? owner.tree.nodes[statement]
                        | .node-assign(line)
                            . name = owner.tree.identifier-name(line.lhs)
                            if name && !property-named(level, name)
                                for member in owner.member-pool[members]
                                    do match? owner.decls[member]
                                        | .decl-property(property)
                                            if property.defaults-root && at-statement
                                                lines += member
                                            .. at-statement = property.syntax == statement
if applications.count == 0 && lines.length == 0
    = order
. home = enter-module(ref.module)
. next = apply-root-written(level, ref, made, order, site, root, applications, lines)
enter-module(home)
= next

────────────────────
_ do enter-module ModuleId
    - entered ModuleId

` Types what follows as written in a module, as the style rules a class of another module
` writes are applied to an object, the diagnostics there being that module's. Answers the
` module typed in before.
. home = module
module = entered
tree = program.modules[entered].tree
frame.module = entered
frame.tree = tree
= home

────────────────────
_ do apply-root-written U32
    - level TypeId
    - ref DeclRef
    - made TypeId
    - order U32
    - site SyntaxId
    - root SyntaxId
    - applications RowRange'SyntaxId
    - lines [DeclId]

` Applies the rules and style lines of the root `<This` of a class, in the module that writes
` it, as `apply-root-rules` says.
. first = facts.style-applications.length
. cells = facts.scope-cells.length as U32
. context = instances.rows[instance].context
. sheeted = markup-sheets.length
. scoped = rule-scopes.length
if context != U32.max
    . held = instances.contexts[context]
    for position in held.first + held.styles .. < held.first + held.styles + held.sheets
        markup-sheets += instances.context-types[position]
        sheet-levels += instances.context-levels[position]
    for position in held.scope-first .. < held.scope-first + held.scopes
        if instances.context-cells[position] == 0 && instances.context-valued[position] == U32.max
            rule-scopes += ScopeUse(instances.context-scopes[position])
. seen [ScopeUse]
for use in element-scopes
    seen += use
. refused = preparing
preparing = preparing.content-refused = true
preparing = preparing.values-once = true
preparing = preparing.site = 0
. next = order
for position in 0 .. < applications.count
    element-scopes.clear()
    . application = tree.children[applications.start + position]
    . values = no-instance
    do match? tree.nodes[application]
        | .node-style-rule-application(applied)
            if applied.args.count != 0
                values = instances.intern-root-values(module, level, application, context)
                demand-body(values)
                panics.note-inlined(instance, values)
    next = apply-written-rules
        - root
        - level
        - RowRange'SyntaxId(applications.start + position, 1)
        - next
        - values
    if next == U32.max
        break
preparing = refused
element-scopes.clear()
for use in seen
    element-scopes += use
while markup-sheets.length > sheeted
    markup-sheets.pop()
    sheet-levels.pop()
while rule-scopes.length > scoped
    rule-scopes.pop()
if next == U32.max
    = U32.max
for index in first .. < facts.style-applications.length
    . cell = facts.style-applications[index].cell
    if cell >= cells && cell < U32.max - 1
        decline(site)
        = U32.max
. empty [ScopeUse]
do prune-cells(cells, empty)
for index in first .. < facts.style-applications.length
    facts.style-applications[index].layer = 0
    revise-application(index as U32)
    if facts.style-applications[index].outer == U32.max
        facts.style-applications[index].made = level
        revise-application(index as U32)
    if facts.style-applications[index].action != no-instance
        facts.style-applications[index].action = demand-style-gates(made)
        revise-application(index as U32)
for member in lines
    . unit = instances.intern-initializer(ref.module, member, level)
    if instances.rows[unit].state == .instance-in-progress
        decline(site)
        = U32.max
    demand-body(unit)
    panics.note-inlined(instance, unit)
    if !note-style-errors(unit, site)
        = U32.max
    . count = facts.style-declaration-count(unit)
    if count == 0
        decline(site)
        = U32.max
    facts.style-applications += StyleApplication(instance, ref.module, root, unit, 0, next)
    facts.style-applications[facts.style-applications.length - 1].made = level
    revise-application((facts.style-applications.length - 1) as U32)
    if facts.authors-in(unit)
        facts.style-applications[facts.style-applications.length - 1].action = demand-style-gates
            - made
        revise-application((facts.style-applications.length - 1) as U32)
    next += count
if next != order
    facts.style-sites += StyleSite(instance, ref.module, root)
= next

────────────────────
+ do check-root-style
    - receiver TypeId
    - row PropertyDecl

` Types a line of a root `<This` that names no property of its class as the declaration of a
` style property of the object, as the reference's constructor declares it among the class's
` defaults (`compileRootThisStyleDefaults`): as a line of the class's rule `• This` is
` (`declare-unit-style`), with `this` bound, at the root.
frame.self-type = receiver
bind-this(receiver)
frame.close-env()
open-class-env(holding-type(receiver, DeclRef(module, row.owner)))
. root = 0u32
do match? program.modules[module].decls[row.owner]
    | .decl-class(class)
        root = tree.root-this(class.content)
. styles = style-vocabulary(receiver, row.syntax)
if styles
    do declare-unit-style(row.syntax, root, receiver, styles, 0)
instances.set-returns(instance, types.void-type, types.void-type, .return-declared)
finish-errors(frame)
close()

────────────────────
_ do queries-markup Bool
    - ref DeclRef
    - written SyntaxId

` Whether the type a class writes for a property is a query of the markup an object is in,
` `Ancestor'T` or `Descendants'T` of the markup runtime, or the optional of one.
. owner = program.modules[ref.module]
. env = types.class-env(ref.module, ref.decl)
. type = types.evaluate-type(ref.module, owner.tree, written, env)
types.env-release(env)
. held = if types.is-optional(type) then types.optional-inner(type) else type
if held == invalid-type || types.intrinsic-of(held) != .class
    = false
. declared = class-ref(types, held)
. home = program.modules[declared.module]
if home.name != "core/markup"
    = false
do match? home.decls[declared.decl]
    | .decl-class(class)
        = class.name.text == "Ancestor" || class.name.text == "Descendants"
= false

────────────────────
_ do using-style TypeId
    - ref DeclRef
    - using UsingDecl
    - site SyntaxId

` The style a class, or an extension of a style sheet, names in a using, or none where the using
` is declined or reported. One of a style sheet is no style (`using-sheet`); `StyleSheet` itself
` is the reference's error.
. used = using-type(ref, using)
. root = types.intrinsic-of(used) == .style-sheet && used == types.type-row(.style-sheet)
if used == invalid-type || (types.intrinsic-of(used) == .style-sheet && !root)
    decline(if ref.module == module then using.syntax else site)
    = no-type
if types.intrinsic-of(used) != .style || used == types.type-row(.style)
    if ref.module != module
        decline(site)
    else
        frame.diagnose
            - using.syntax
            - .stated
            - program.store-atom("Using target must be a Style or StyleSheet")
    = no-type
= used

────────────────────
_ do using-sheet TypeId
    - ref DeclRef
    - using UsingDecl

` The style sheet a class names in a using, declared `• Name`, or none.
. used = using-type(ref, using)
types.clear-fault()
if used == invalid-type || types.intrinsic-of(used) != .style-sheet
    = no-type
. sheet = class-ref(types, used)
= if is-sheet-decl(sheet.module, sheet.decl) then family-root(used) else no-type

────────────────────
_ do using-type TypeId
    - ref DeclRef
    - using UsingDecl

` The type a using of a class or of an extension of a style sheet names, with the fault the
` type store gives where it names none. One it names is kept, and found again as it was.
. key = ((ref.module as Size) /lshift/ 32) /or/ (using.type-syntax as Size)
. known = session.scratch.using-types[key]
if known
    types.clear-fault()
    = known
. owner = program.modules[ref.module]
. env = holder-env(ref)
types.clear-fault()
. used = types.evaluate-type(ref.module, owner.tree, using.type-syntax, env)
types.env-release(env)
if used != invalid-type
    session.scratch.using-types[key] = used
= used

────────────────────
+ do add-sheet-groups
    - class TypeId
    - sheets [TypeId]
    - levels [U32]

` Adds the style sheets a class uses to those seen, each in its group, as the reference's
` `visibleStyleSheetUsingGroups` and `addStyleSheetVocabularyGroup` add them: the classes of its
` chain, base first, each a group of its own, higher than those before, each sheet only where it
` is first seen. The sheets of each class of the chain are found once (`chain-sheets`).
if class == no-type || class == invalid-type || types.intrinsic-of(class) != .class
    =
. place = chain-sheets(class) as Size
. position = U32.max
. group = 0u32
while facts.chain-sheets[place] != no-type
    . sheet = facts.chain-sheets[place]
    if facts.chain-sheet-positions[place] != position
        position = facts.chain-sheet-positions[place]
        group = if levels.length != 0 then levels[levels.length - 1] + 1 else 0
    if sheets.find(sheet) == null
        sheets += sheet
        levels += group
    place += 1

────────────────────
_ do chain-sheets U32
    - class TypeId

` Where the style sheets the classes of a chain use begin in `chain-sheets`, each with the place of
` its class in the chain, base first, in the order the classes name them, ended by none; found the
` first time they are asked for.
. held = facts.chain-sheet-places[class]
=? held if held
. start = facts.chain-sheets.length as U32
. chain [TypeId]
. level TypeId? = class
while level && types.intrinsic-of(level) == .class
    chain += level
    level = types.base-of(level)
for position in 0 .. < chain.length
    for ref in sheet-parts(class-ref(types, chain[chain.length - 1 - position]))
        . owner = program.modules[ref.module]
        for member in owner.member-pool[part-members(ref)]
            do match? owner.decls[member]
                | .decl-using(using)
                    . sheet = using-sheet(ref, using)
                    if sheet != no-type
                        facts.chain-sheets += sheet
                        facts.chain-sheet-positions += position as U32
facts.chain-sheets += no-type
facts.chain-sheet-positions += U32.max
facts.chain-sheet-places[class] = start
= start

────────────────────
+ sheets-known Bool

` Whether the style sheets markup written here sees are known here: in the main code of a module,
` or a function or a property's getter or setter that is nested in none, as the reference starts
` such a function with none; in the function that makes a class's content, which is one of its
` own for those of the markup that makes the object (`load-context`); and in a function that
` builds markup the markup around it gives them to (`sheets-given`); and in a constructor, whose
` body the reference starts with none and whose defaults it applies under those of the markup
` that makes the object (`apply-style-defaults`). Another nested in one sees those of the markup
` around it.
|? frame.declaration.is-content || sheets-given
    true
??
    instances.rows[instance].enclosing == no-instance && (kind == .main-decl || kind == .function-decl || kind == .getter-decl || kind == .setter-decl || is-constructor-kind(kind))

.. kind = frame.declaration.kind

────────────────────
+ do seen-sheets
    - sheets [TypeId]
    - levels [U32]

` The style sheets markup written here sees where no element is around it, in their groups,
` those of the class it is written in, or `sheet-self` while the way to a slot outlet is followed,
` where there are none.
for sheet in markup-sheets
    sheets += sheet
for level in sheet-levels
    levels += level
if sheets.length == 0
    add-sheet-groups(if keying.sheet-self != no-type then keying.sheet-self else frame.self-type, sheets, levels)

────────────────────
+ do defaults-apply-rules Bool
    - class TypeId

` Whether the rule `• This` of a class of a chain applies rules, as the reference's
` `styleDefaultsApplyRules` asks.
. level TypeId? = class
while level && types.intrinsic-of(level) == .class
    . ref = class-ref(types, level)
    . owner = program.modules[ref.module]
    do match? owner.decls[ref.decl]
        | .decl-class(declared)
            for member in owner.member-pool[declared.members]
                do match? owner.decls[member]
                    | .decl-style-rule(rule)
                        if rule.name.text == "This" && owner.tree.applies-rules(rule.syntax)
                            = true
    level = types.base-of(level)
= false

────────────────────
+ do sheet-has-slot Bool
    - sheet TypeId
    - name Atom

` Whether a style sheet declares a slot of a name.
. ref = class-ref(types, sheet)
. owner = program.modules[ref.module]
do match? owner.decls[ref.decl]
    | .decl-class(declared)
        for member in owner.member-pool[declared.members]
            do match? owner.decls[member]
                | .decl-property(property)
                    if property.name && property.name == name
                        = true
= false

────────────────────
+ do names-sheet-slot Bool
    - name Atom

` Whether any style sheet of the program declares a slot of a name, among the names gathered
` once (`list-sheet-slots`).
list-sheet-slots()
= facts.sheet-slot-names[name] != null

────────────────────
_ do list-sheet-slots

=? if facts.slot-names-listed
facts.slot-names-listed = true
for position in 0 .. < program.modules.length
    . owner = program.modules[position]
    for index in 0 .. < owner.decls.length
        do match? owner.decls[index]
            | .decl-property(property)
                if property.name && property.owner != 0 && in-sheet
                    facts.sheet-slot-names[property.name] = 1
                .. in-sheet = is-sheet-decl(position as ModuleId, property.owner)

────────────────────
_ do declare-sheet-slot U32
    - statement SyntaxId
    - element SyntaxId
    - index U32
    - position U32
    - layer U32
    - order U32
    - value SyntaxId
    - made TypeId

` A style declaration whose value is a name alone that names a slot of a style sheet the element
` sees, as the reference's `compileStyleDeclaration` takes one: the runtime reads the slot's
` value as it settles. The sheets the element sees are in groups, lowest first: those the class
` the markup is written in uses, those of the elements it is in, outermost first, then those of
` the element's class (`add-sheet-groups`); the slot is that of the highest group that has one
` of the name, and two in one group are the reference's error. A name that is also a local, a
` global, or a member of the class the markup is written in or of an element it is in is the
` reference's error. Answers 0 where the value names no such slot, 1 where it is declared, and 2
` where it is reported or declined. Where the sheets the markup sees are not known here
` (`sheets-known`), a name that is a slot of any style sheet is declined, as is a slot of another
` type than the property's.
. name Atom? = null
do match? tree.nodes[value]
    | .node-identifier(row)
        if !row.is-tracked
            name = row.name
if !name || types.well-known-type("core/style", "StyleSheetInfo") == invalid-type
    = 0
if !sheets-known()
    if names-sheet-slot(name)
        decline(statement)
        = 2
    = 0
. (found, resolved) = resolve-slot(made, name, module, statement)
if !resolved
    = 2
if found == no-type
    = 0
. clashes = (resolution-flags /and/ ResolutionFlag.resolution-styled) == 0
    .. resolution-flags = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, value).flags
for parent in content-parents
    if property-named(parent, name) || declares-event(parent, name)
        clashes = true
if self-class && (self-property || declares-event(frame.self-type, name))
    clashes = true
.. self-property = property-named(frame.self-type, name)
.. self-class = frame.self-type != no-type && types.intrinsic-of(frame.self-type) == .class
if clashes
    . text = "\"${name.text}\" is ambiguous: it names both a StyleSheet slot of ${type-short-name(types, found)} and a lexical value"
    frame.diagnose(value, .stated, program.store-atom(text))
    = 2
= declare-slot(statement, element, index, position, layer, order, value, name, found)

────────────────────
_ do bind-rule-slots Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - made TypeId
    - unit InstanceId
    - application U32

` Resolves, where a style rule a class writes is applied to a markup element, each line whose
` value is a name alone that a style sheet may answer against the sheets the element sees, as
` the reference resolves it there (`resolve-slot`): a line whose name nothing else declares
` takes that slot's value (`rule-slots`), and one whose name is also a value the rule sees is
` the reference's error. Declined: such a name no sheet the element sees answers, and one
` where the sheets are not known here.
. owner = instances.rows[unit].module
. written = program.modules[owner].tree
. count = facts.style-declarations.length as U32
. place = facts.first-style-declaration(unit)
while place < count
    . row = facts.style-declarations[place]
    place = facts.next-style-declaration(place)
    if row.inherits
        continue
    . value SyntaxId = 0
    do match? written.nodes[row.site]
        | .node-assign(line)
            value = line.rhs
    . name Atom? = null
    do match? written.nodes[value]
        | .node-identifier(ident)
            if !ident.is-tracked
                name = ident.name
    . deferred = row.sheet == U32.max - 1
    if !name || !names-sheet-slot(name)
        if deferred
            decline(id)
            = false
        continue
    if !sheets-known()
        decline(id)
        = false
    . (found, resolved) = resolve-slot(made, name, owner, row.site)
    if !resolved
        = false
    if found == no-type
        if deferred
            decline(id)
            = false
        continue
    if !deferred
        report-at(owner, value, "\"${name.text}\" is ambiguous: it names both a StyleSheet slot of ${type-short-name(types, found)} and a lexical value")
        = false
    . (number, offset, projection) = slot-binding(owner, row.site, row.property, value, name, found, id)
    if number == U32.max
        = false
    revise-application(application)
    facts.add-rule-slot(RuleSlot(application, row.site, number, offset, projection))
= true

────────────────────
_ do defers-slot Bool
    - value SyntaxId

` Whether the value of a line of a style rule a class writes is a name alone that nothing
` declares and some style sheet has a slot of, which is resolved where the rule is applied
` (`bind-rule-slots`).
do match? tree.nodes[value]
    | .node-identifier(row)
        = !row.is-tracked && (bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, value).flags /and/ ResolutionFlag.resolution-styled) != 0 && names-sheet-slot(row.name)
= false

────────────────────
+ do visible-sheets
    - made TypeId
    - sheets [TypeId]
    - levels [U32]

` The style sheets a markup element of a class sees, each in its group, lowest first, as the
` reference's `styleSheetVocabularyGroupsFor` gives them: those of the markup the element is
` in, or where there are none those the class the markup is written in uses, then those of the
` element's class (`add-sheet-groups`), but at a slot outlet (`overlaying`), where the reference
` adds none.
seen-sheets(sheets, levels)
if !preparing.overlaying
    add-sheet-groups(made, sheets, levels)

────────────────────
_ do declare-own-slot U32
    - statement SyntaxId
    - element SyntaxId
    - index U32
    - position U32
    - order U32
    - value SyntaxId
    - sheet TypeId

` A line of a rule of a style sheet whose value is a name alone that names a slot of the sheet,
` which the reference resolves against that sheet alone: declared as `declare-slot` says.
` Answers as `declare-sheet-slot` does.
do match? tree.nodes[value]
    | .node-identifier(row)
        if !row.is-tracked && sheet-has-slot(sheet, row.name)
            = declare-slot(statement, element, index, position, 0, order, value, row.name, sheet)
= 0

────────────────────
_ do reads-sheet-member Bool
    - value SyntaxId
    - sheet TypeId

` Whether a value a rule of a style sheet declares names `this` or a member of the sheet that is
` no slot of it, which the reference compiles with no object of the sheet.
. root = family-root(sheet)
for node in tree.subtree-start(value) .. value
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-identifier(row)
            if row.name.text == "this" || (property-named(sheet, row.name) && not-slot)
                = true
            .. not-slot = !sheet-has-slot(root, row.name)
= false

────────────────────
_ do enter-theme ThemeScope
    - made TypeId
    - sheet TypeId
    - statement SyntaxId

. outer = ThemeScope(theme-made, theme-sheet, theme-statement, theme-number)
theme-made = made
theme-sheet = sheet
theme-statement = statement
theme-number = U32.max
= outer

────────────────────
_ do leave-theme U32
    - outer ThemeScope

. number = theme-number
theme-made = outer.made
theme-sheet = outer.sheet
theme-statement = outer.statement
theme-number = outer.number
= number

────────────────────
+ do read-theme TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - name Atom

. found = no-type
if theme-sheet != no-type
    found = sheet-slot-owner(theme-sheet, name)
else
    if !sheets-known()
        decline(id)
        = invalid-type
    . (seen, resolved) = resolve-slot(theme-made, name, module, theme-statement)
    if !resolved
        = invalid-type
    found = seen
if found == no-type
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("Name not found"))
    = invalid-type
. number = sheet-index(family-root(found), module, theme-statement, id)
if number == U32.max
    = invalid-type
. use = facts.style-sheet-uses[number]
. offset = 0u32
while offset < use.count && facts.sheet-slots[use.first + offset].name != name
    offset += 1
if offset == use.count
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
if theme-number != U32.max && theme-number != number
    . other = type-short-name(types, facts.style-sheet-uses[theme-number].type)
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("A style value reads slots of one StyleSheet: \"${name.text}\" is a slot of ${type-short-name(types, use.type)}, and others it reads are slots of $other"))
    = invalid-type
theme-number = number
facts.add-theme-read(ThemeRead(instance, module, id, number, offset))
= facts.sheet-slots[use.first + offset].type

────────────────────
_ do sheet-slot-owner TypeId
    - sheet TypeId
    - name Atom

. root = family-root(sheet)
=? root if sheet-has-slot(root, name)
for part in sheet-parts(class-ref(types, root))
    . owner = program.modules[part.module]
    for member in owner.member-pool[part-members(part)]
        do match? owner.decls[member]
            | .decl-using(using)
                . used = using-sheet(part, using)
                if used != no-type && sheet-has-slot(used, name)
                    = used
= no-type

────────────────────
_ do theme-static Bool
    - value SyntaxId

for node in tree.subtree-start(value) .. value
    if facts.theme-read-of(instance, node)
        continue
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-style-read-expression
            = false
        | .node-identifier(row)
            if row.is-tracked || row.name.text == "this"
                = false
            . kind = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, node).kind
            if kind == .resolve-slot || kind == .resolve-member
                = false
= true

────────────────────
_ do declare-themed Bool
    - statement SyntaxId
    - element SyntaxId
    - index U32
    - position U32
    - layer U32
    - order U32
    - value SyntaxId
    - number U32

. property = facts.style-properties[position]
if is-live-statement(statement) || !theme-static(value)
    frame.diagnose(value, .stated, program.store-atom("A style value that reads StyleSheet slots may read no local, member, style or tracked value; read a slot as \"\$name\" to compute with one"))
    = false
if !demand-themed-runtime()
    decline(statement)
    = false
. place = facts.note-themed-value(module, statement, instance, property.type, number)
. declaration = StyleDeclaration
    - instance
    - element
    - statement
    - facts.style-uses[index].type
    - position
    - layer
    - order
    - false
declaration.themed = place
facts.add-style-declaration(declaration)
= true

────────────────────
_ do demand-themed-runtime Bool

. runtime = facts.style-runtime
if runtime.site-themed != no-instance
    = true
if !demand-sheet-declarations()
    = false
runtime = facts.style-runtime
. module-id = class-ref(types, types.type-row(.style)).module
. info = types.well-known-type("core/style", "StyleInfo")
. sheet = types.well-known-type("core/style", "StyleSheetInfo")
. record = types.well-known-type("core/style", "StyleSheetRecord")
. maker = types.well-known-type("core/style", "StyleThemedMaker")
. made = types.well-known-type("core/style", "StyleOptionalBits")
if info-missing || record == invalid-type || maker == invalid-type || made == invalid-type
    = false
.. info-missing = info == invalid-type || sheet == invalid-type
runtime.themed-made = made
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(types.size-type)
scratch.types.push(info)
scratch.types.push(types.size-type)
scratch.types.push(types.type-row(.uint32))
scratch.types.push(types.type-row(.uint32))
scratch.types.push(sheet)
scratch.types.push(types.size-type)
scratch.types.push(maker)
runtime.site-themed = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - module-id
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("style-template-site-themed")
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
scratch.types.push(record)
scratch.types.push(types.size-type)
runtime.themed-slot = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - module-id
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("style-themed-slot")
    - mark
runtime.themed-none = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - module-id
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("style-themed-none")
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
facts.style-runtime = runtime
= themed-ready && runtime.themed-none != no-instance
    .. themed-ready = runtime.site-themed != no-instance && runtime.themed-slot != no-instance

────────────────────
_ do demand-family-runtime Bool

. runtime = facts.style-runtime
if runtime.site-family != no-instance
    = true
if !demand-sheet-declarations()
    = false
runtime = facts.style-runtime
. module-id = class-ref(types, types.type-row(.style)).module
. sheet = types.well-known-type("core/style", "StyleSheetInfo")
if sheet == invalid-type
    = false
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(types.size-type)
scratch.types.push(sheet)
scratch.types.push(types.type-row(.uint64))
runtime.site-family = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - module-id
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("style-template-site-family")
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
scratch.types.push(types.size-type)
runtime.site-family-end = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - module-id
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("style-template-site-family-end")
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
facts.style-runtime = runtime
= runtime.site-family != no-instance && runtime.site-family-end != no-instance

────────────────────
_ do declare-slot U32
    - statement SyntaxId
    - element SyntaxId
    - index U32
    - position U32
    - layer U32
    - order U32
    - value SyntaxId
    - name Atom
    - found TypeId

` Records a declaration that takes its value from a slot of a style sheet (`slot-binding`).
` Answers as `declare-sheet-slot` does.
if layer == U32.max
    decline(statement)
    = 2
. (number, offset, projection) = slot-binding(module, statement, position, value, name, found, statement)
if number == U32.max
    = 2
facts.add-style-declaration
    - StyleDeclaration
        - instance
        - element
        - statement
        - facts.style-uses[index].type
        - position
        - layer
        - order
        - true
        - false
        - false
        - number
        - offset
        - projection
= 1

────────────────────
_ do slot-binding (U32, U32, U32)
    - owner ModuleId
    - statement SyntaxId
    - position U32
    - value SyntaxId
    - name Atom
    - found TypeId
    - at SyntaxId

` The number of the style sheet whose slot of a name a declaration of a style property takes
` its value from, written at `statement` in a module, the slot's place among the sheet's, and
` how its bits become the property's where their types differ (`sheet-projection`), or
` `U32.max`; with the reference's errors where they cannot, and declined at `at`. The number is
` `U32.max` where it is reported or declined.
. number = sheet-index(family-root(found), owner, statement, at)
if number == U32.max
    = (U32.max, 0, 0)
. use = facts.style-sheet-uses[number]
. offset = 0u32
while offset < use.count && facts.sheet-slots[use.first + offset].name != name
    offset += 1
. property = facts.style-properties[position]
if offset == use.count || !demand-style-sites() || !demand-sheet-declarations()
    decline(at)
    = (U32.max, 0, 0)
. slot = facts.sheet-slots[use.first + offset]
. projection = U32.max
if slot.type != property.type
    if !relation-legal(relations.compare(slot.type, property.type, false, false, null, owner))
        report-at(owner, value, "StyleSheet slot \"${name.text}\" has type ${type-display(types, slot.type)}, which cannot be converted to style property \"${property.name.text}\" type ${type-display(types, property.type)}")
        facts.mention-types([slot.type, property.type])
        = (U32.max, 0, 0)
    projection = sheet-projection(slot.type, property.type)
    if projection == U32.max - 1
        . shown = type-display(types, property.type)
        report-at(owner, value, "StyleSheet slot \"${name.text}\" can convert to $shown, but not as a zero-allocation style-sheet projection; declare the slot as $shown or assign a concrete value.")
        facts.mention-types([property.type])
        = (U32.max, 0, 0)
    if projection == U32.max
        decline(at)
        = (U32.max, 0, 0)
= (number, offset, projection)

────────────────────
_ do sheet-projection U32
    - source TypeId
    - target TypeId

` How the runtime makes the bits of a style property's value of those of a slot of a style sheet
` of another type, as the reference's `styleSheetProjectionPlan` says, recorded among
` `style-projections`: where the slot is no optional or the property is one, the bits of what an
` optional slot holds are copied where the property's type takes them as they are, or wrapped as
` the case of a union the property holds that takes them so (`reusable-case`), or of a union slot
` whose every case's value a case of the property's union takes so, given that case's number
` (`style-projection-union-remap`), whose table program tables number in source order
` (`ProgramTables.remap-number`). A case wraps the slot's bits only where they fit above its
` number: a whole number of at most 32 bits, or a handle; not a wider number such as a float.
` `U32.max - 1` where there is no such way, the reference's error.
if types.is-optional(source) && !types.is-optional(target)
    = U32.max - 1
. held = if types.is-optional(source) then types.optional-inner(source) else source
. wanted = if types.is-optional(target) then types.optional-inner(target) else target
. preserves = types.is-optional(source) && types.is-optional(target)
if !demand-sheet-projections()
    = U32.max
. index = facts.style-projections.length as U32
if reuses-style-bits(held, wanted)
    facts.style-projections += StyleProjection(0, 0, preserves)
    = index
if types.intrinsic-of(wanted) != .union
    = U32.max - 1
. found = reusable-case(held, wanted)
if found != U32.max
    . payload = types.cases-of(wanted)[found].type
    if !inline-style-case(payload) && !holds-handle(payload)
        = U32.max - 1
    facts.style-projections += StyleProjection(1, found, preserves)
    = index
if types.intrinsic-of(held) == .union
    . sources = types.cases-of(held)
    . first = facts.projection-tags.length as U32
    for position in 0 .. < sources.length
        . item = sources[position]
        . tag = if item.is-default then U32.max else reusable-case(item.type, wanted)
        if tag == U32.max
            -= facts.projection-tags[first .. < facts.projection-tags.length]
            = U32.max - 1
        facts.projection-tags += tag
    facts.style-projections += StyleProjection
        - 2
        - sources.length as U32
        - preserves
        - first
        - sources.length as U32
    = index
= U32.max - 1

────────────────────
_ reuses-style-bits Bool
    - source TypeId
    - target TypeId

` Whether the bits of a style value of one type are those of another's, as the reference's
` `styleProjectionCanReusePayloadBits` says: the same type, or an object of a class below the
` other's.
|? source == target
    true
??
    both-classes && in-base-chain(types, source, target)

.. both-classes = types.intrinsic-of(source) == .class && types.intrinsic-of(target) == .class

────────────────────
_ do reusable-case U32
    - source TypeId
    - union TypeId

` The case of a union whose value takes the bits of a style value of another type as they are,
` as the reference's `styleProjectionReusableUnionCase` chooses it: one of the same type before
` one of a class above it, the first of each. None where no case does.
. found = U32.max
. cases = types.cases-of(union)
for index in 0 .. < cases.length
    . item = cases[index]
    if item.is-default || item.type == no-type || item.type == types.void-type
        continue
    if item.type == source
        = index as U32
    if found == U32.max && reuses-style-bits(source, item.type)
        found = index as U32
= found

────────────────────
_ do demand-sheet-projections Bool

` The function of the style runtime that declares the slot of a style sheet as a style's value of
` another type for a site, typed once.
. runtime = facts.style-runtime
if runtime.site-projected != no-instance
    = true
. module-id = class-ref(types, types.type-row(.style)).module
. info = types.well-known-type("core/style", "StyleInfo")
. sheet = types.well-known-type("core/style", "StyleSheetInfo")
. tags = types.well-known-type-of("core", "ConstArray", types.type-row(.uint8))
if tags == invalid-type
    = false
. remap = types.optional-of(tags)
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(types.size-type)
scratch.types.push(info)
scratch.types.push(types.size-type)
scratch.types.push(types.type-row(.uint32))
scratch.types.push(types.type-row(.uint32))
scratch.types.push(sheet)
scratch.types.push(types.size-type)
scratch.types.push(types.type-row(.uint32))
scratch.types.push(types.type-row(.int64))
scratch.types.push(types.size-type)
scratch.types.push(types.bool-type)
scratch.types.push(remap)
runtime.site-projected = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - module-id
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("style-template-site-style-sheet-projected")
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
runtime.remap-tags = remap
facts.style-runtime = runtime
= runtime.site-projected != no-instance

────────────────────
_ do slot-domains U32
    - ref DeclRef
    - name Atom
    - home ModuleId
    - site SyntaxId

. owner = program.modules[ref.module]
. mask = 0u32
do match? owner.decls[ref.decl]
    | .decl-class(declared)
        for member in owner.member-pool[declared.members]
            do match? owner.decls[member]
                | .decl-style-domains(domains)
                    do match? owner.tree.nodes[domains.syntax]
                        | .node-style-annotation(row)
                            if owner.tree.identifier-name(row.left) == name
                                for item in owner.tree.children[row.domains]
                                    do match? owner.tree.nodes[item]
                                        | .node-style-domain-item(domain)
                                            . named = owner.tree.identifier-name(domain.domain)
                                            if named && domain.target == 0
                                                . index = style-domain
                                                    - named
                                                    - home
                                                    - site
                                                    - ref.module
                                                    - item
                                                if index < 32
                                                    mask = mask /or/ (1u32 /lshift/ (index as Size))
= mask

────────────────────
+ do check-sheet-domains
    - index DeclId
    - class ClassDecl

. mark = scratch.types.mark
. sheet = types.intern-class(module, index, mark)
types.complete(sheet)
. base = types.base-of(sheet) ?? no-type
for member in program.modules[module].member-pool[class.members]
    do match? program.modules[module].decls[member]
        | .decl-style-domains(domains)
            do match? tree.nodes[domains.syntax]
                | .node-style-annotation(row)
                    . name = tree.identifier-name(row.left)
                    if is-sheet-type(base)
                        frame.diagnose(domains.syntax, .stated, program.store-atom("Derived StyleSheet \"${class.name.text}\" names no domains; its slots raise those ${type-short-name(types, family-root(sheet))} names"))
                    else if !name || !sheet-has-slot(sheet, name)
                        frame.diagnose(row.left, .stated, program.store-atom("StyleSheet slot \"${if name then name.text else ""}\" does not exist"))
                    else
                        for item in tree.children[row.domains]
                            do match? tree.nodes[item]
                                | .node-style-domain-item(domain)
                                    if domain.target != 0
                                        frame.diagnose(domain.target, .stated, program.store-atom("A StyleSheet slot raises its domains on the node that reads it, so they name no target"))

────────────────────
_ do sheet-index U32
    - sheet TypeId
    - home ModuleId
    - site SyntaxId
    - at SyntaxId

` The number of a style sheet among those the program registers, given when a declaration
` first takes a value from one of its slots, with its slots in the order the sheet declares
` them, each kept in a stored property of the object its constructor makes and becoming bits as
` a property of a style does; or none where it is declined, at `at`. The declaration is written
` at `site` in a module, and is noted as the instance's use of the sheet (`note-style-user`). Its
` constructor takes nothing.
for position in 0 .. < facts.style-sheet-uses.length
    if facts.style-sheet-uses[position].type == sheet
        facts.lookups += 1
        place-sheet-domains(sheet, home, site)
        note-style-user(sheet, home, site, false)
        = position as U32
. ref = class-ref(types, sheet)
. owner = program.modules[ref.module]
. first = facts.sheet-slots.length as U32
do match? owner.decls[ref.decl]
    | .decl-class(declared)
        for member in owner.member-pool[declared.members]
            do match? owner.decls[member]
                | .decl-property(property)
                    if !property.name
                        continue
                    . named = property.name
                    . seen = false
                    . start Size = first
                    for place in start .. < facts.sheet-slots.length
                        if facts.sheet-slots[place].name == named
                            seen = true
                    if seen
                        continue
                    . found = property-named(sheet, named)
                    if !found
                        decline(at)
                        = U32.max
                    . row = types.properties[found]
                    . declared-type = if untyped then demand-member(row, sheet, named) else row.type
                        .. untyped = row.type == no-type
                    if row.storage-kind != .storage-eager || unresolved
                        decline(at)
                        = U32.max
                    .. unresolved = declared-type == invalid-type || declared-type == no-type
                    . flags = sheet-slot-flags(declared-type)
                    if flags == U32.max
                        decline(at)
                        = U32.max
                    facts.sheet-slots += SheetSlot
                        - named
                        - declared-type
                        - row.slot
                        - flags
                        - slot-domains(ref, named, home, site)
. mark = scratch.types.mark
. singleton = calls.demand-constructor(sheet, mark)
. last = facts.sheet-slots.length as U32
if singleton == no-instance || !demand-sheet-runtime() || !demand-sheet-members(sheet, first, last)
    decline(at)
    = U32.max
. index = facts.style-sheet-uses.length as U32
facts.style-sheet-uses += StyleSheetUse(sheet, singleton, first, last - first)
note-style-user(sheet, home, site, false)
= index

────────────────────
_ do place-sheet-domains
    - sheet TypeId
    - home ModuleId
    - site SyntaxId

` Places the domains the slots of a style sheet name, as a later use of the sheet at `site` in
` `home` names each (`place-style-domain`) as its first use does (`slot-domains`), so that the
` places noted do not depend on which instance used the sheet first.
. ref = class-ref(types, sheet)
. owner = program.modules[ref.module]
do match? owner.decls[ref.decl]
    | .decl-class(declared)
        for member in owner.member-pool[declared.members]
            do match? owner.decls[member]
                | .decl-style-domains(domains)
                    do match? owner.tree.nodes[domains.syntax]
                        | .node-style-annotation(row)
                            for item in owner.tree.children[row.domains]
                                do match? owner.tree.nodes[item]
                                    | .node-style-domain-item(domain)
                                        . named = owner.tree.identifier-name(domain.domain)
                                        if named && domain.target == 0
                                            place-style-domain(named, home, site, ref.module, item)

────────────────────
_ do demand-sheet-members Bool
    - sheet TypeId
    - first U32
    - last U32

list-derived-sheets()
for derived in facts.derived-sheets
    if family-root(derived) != sheet
        continue
    . start = facts.sheet-member-slots.length as U32
    . level = derived
    while true
        . ref = class-ref(types, level)
        . owner = program.modules[ref.module]
        do match? owner.decls[ref.decl]
            | .decl-class(declared)
                for member in owner.member-pool[declared.members]
                    do match? owner.decls[member]
                        | .decl-property(property)
                            . named = property.name
                            if named && (level != sheet || (property.value != 0 && slot-reads))
                                add-member-slot(named, start, first, last)
                            .. slot-reads = reads-sheet-slots(owner.tree, property.value, sheet)
        if level == sheet
            break
        level = types.base-of(level) ?? sheet
    . mark = scratch.types.mark
    . singleton = calls.demand-constructor(derived, mark)
    if singleton == no-instance || !demand-sheet-member-runtime()
        = false
    facts.sheet-members += SheetMember
        - sheet
        - derived
        - singleton
        - start
        - (facts.sheet-member-slots.length as U32) - start
= true

────────────────────
_ do reads-sheet-slots Bool
    - written AST
    - value SyntaxId
    - sheet TypeId

for node in written.subtree-start(value) .. value
    do match? written.nodes[node]
        | .node-identifier(row)
            if row.name.text == "this" || sheet-has-slot(sheet, row.name)
                = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do add-member-slot
    - name Atom
    - start U32
    - first U32
    - last U32

for place in first .. < last
    if facts.sheet-slots[place].name == name
        . offset = place - first
        for held in (start as Size) .. < facts.sheet-member-slots.length
            if facts.sheet-member-slots[held] == offset
                =
        facts.sheet-member-slots += offset
        =

────────────────────
_ do demand-sheet-member-runtime Bool

. runtime = facts.style-runtime
if runtime.sheet-member-slot != no-instance
    = true
. module-id = class-ref(types, types.type-row(.style)).module
. info = types.well-known-type("core/style", "StyleSheetInfo")
. record = types.well-known-type("core/style", "StyleSheetRecord")
if info == invalid-type || record == invalid-type
    = false
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(info)
scratch.types.push(types.string-type)
scratch.types.push(types.string-type)
scratch.types.push(types.type-row(.uint32))
scratch.types.push(types.type-row(.uint32))
runtime.sheet-register-member = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - module-id
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("style-sheet-register-member")
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
scratch.types.push(record)
scratch.types.push(types.size-type)
scratch.types.push(types.type-row(.int64))
scratch.types.push(types.bool-type)
runtime.sheet-member-slot = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - module-id
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("style-sheet-member-slot")
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
scratch.types.push(record)
scratch.types.push(types.string-type)
runtime.sheet-member-tag = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - module-id
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("style-sheet-member-tag")
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
facts.style-runtime = runtime
= registers && runtime.sheet-member-slot != no-instance && runtime.sheet-member-tag != no-instance
    .. registers = runtime.sheet-register-member != no-instance

────────────────────
_ do sheet-slot-flags U32
    - type TypeId

` How the bits of a slot of a style sheet are flagged, as the reference's `styleEncodedFlagBits`
` says: 2 where they encode a value of a union, or one boxed, else 0; the values are made bits
` as those of a style's properties are. None for a type that has no such bits.
. held = if types.is-optional(type) then types.optional-inner(type) else type
. kind = types.intrinsic-of(held)
if kind == .union
    for item in types.cases-of(held)
        if style-case(item.type) == U32.max
            = U32.max
    = 2
if intrinsic-is-numeric(kind) && kind != .cpointer && kind != .number
    = 0
if kind == .class
    = if demand-style-coding(held, true) then 0 else U32.max
if boxed-style(kind)
    = if demand-style-coding(held, false) then 2 else U32.max
= U32.max

────────────────────
_ do demand-sheet-runtime Bool

` The functions of the style runtime that registering style sheets calls, typed once.
. runtime = facts.style-runtime
if runtime.sheet-register != no-instance
    = true
if !demand-style-runtime() || !demand-style-sites()
    = false
runtime = facts.style-runtime
. module-id = class-ref(types, types.type-row(.style)).module
. info = types.well-known-type("core/style", "StyleSheetInfo")
if info == invalid-type
    = false
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(types.string-type)
runtime.sheet-info-for = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - module-id
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("style-sheet-info-for")
    - mark
scratch.types.push(types.string-type)
scratch.types.push(types.size-type)
runtime.sheet-info = calls.demand-constructor(info, mark)
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
scratch.types.push(info)
scratch.types.push(types.size-type)
scratch.types.push(types.string-type)
scratch.types.push(types.type-row(.int64))
scratch.types.push(types.bool-type)
scratch.types.push(types.type-row(.uint32))
scratch.types.push(types.type-row(.uint32))
runtime.sheet-register-slot = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - module-id
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("style-sheet-register-slot")
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
scratch.types.push(info)
scratch.types.push(types.type-row(.int64))
runtime.sheet-register = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - module-id
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("style-sheet-register")
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
scratch.types.push(types.index-type)
runtime.sheet-info-required = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - module-id
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("style-sheet-info-required")
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
facts.style-runtime = runtime
= runtime.sheet-info-for != no-instance && runtime.sheet-info != no-instance && runtime.sheet-register-slot != no-instance && runtime.sheet-register != no-instance && runtime.sheet-info-required != no-instance

────────────────────
_ do demand-sheet-declarations Bool

` The function of the style runtime that declares the slot of a style sheet as a style's value
` for a site, typed once.
. runtime = facts.style-runtime
if runtime.site-sheet != no-instance
    = true
. module-id = class-ref(types, types.type-row(.style)).module
. info = types.well-known-type("core/style", "StyleInfo")
. sheet = types.well-known-type("core/style", "StyleSheetInfo")
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(types.size-type)
scratch.types.push(info)
scratch.types.push(types.size-type)
scratch.types.push(types.type-row(.uint32))
scratch.types.push(types.type-row(.uint32))
scratch.types.push(sheet)
scratch.types.push(types.size-type)
runtime.site-sheet = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - module-id
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("style-template-site-style-sheet")
