────────────────────
_ do applied-gate StyleWhen?
    - condition SyntaxId
    - made TypeId

` The condition a style rule written after `•` on a markup element is applied under, which gates
` what the rule declares and the rules it applies, as the reference's `compileStyleGatedBlock`
` gates them: a name or a member read tracked, or the latest value of one, as the reference
` reports, of type `Bool`, tested where each gate is made and again by the function written for
` it (`check-gate-test`). The gate it makes alone is recorded once (`StyleGate`). None where it
` is reported or declined.
if !tree.is-condition-reference(condition)
    frame.diagnose(condition, .stated, program.store-atom("Style rule conditions must be a tracked boolean property reference (like #is-disabled)"))
    = null
. type = infer(condition)
if type == invalid-type
    = null
if type != types.bool-type
    frame.diagnose(condition, .stated, program.store-atom("Style rule conditions must be Bool, but this condition is ${type-display(types, type)}"), type)
    = null
. decl = nested-decl-of(condition)
. test = if decl != 0 then demand-lambda(intern-nested(decl), scratch.no-types) else no-instance
if test == no-instance || instances.signatures[test].errors.count != 0
    decline(condition)
    = null
facts.live-statements += LiveStatement(instance, condition, test)
instances.mark-may-panic(instance)
. action = demand-style-gates(made)
if action == no-instance || instances.live.track == no-instance
    decline(condition)
    = null
. held = StyleWhen(module, condition, U32.max, test)
. whens [StyleWhen]
whens += held
record-gate(made, whens, action)
= held

────────────────────
+ do choose-written-rule Bool
    - made TypeId
    - application SyntaxId
    - given [TypeId]
    - levels [TypeId]
    - members [DeclRef]
    - gates [U64]
    - scoped [ScopeUse]

` The rules a style rule written after `•` applies by its name, for an object of the class `made`
` and the types of the values it gives: the one the class's chain chooses, as the reference's
` `resolveMatch` does, or else those the style sheets in view choose, each with the class that
` writes it, in `levels` and `members`; then those of the rules written in rules in view
` (`element-scopes`) in `scoped`. A name that some rule takes but none for those values is the
` reference's error, and so is a name no module of the program declares (`style-declared`); more than one rule given values, a rule that matches ambiguously, and a
` choice the sheets or the rules in view cannot make here are declined. False where one is.
do match? tree.nodes[application]
    | .node-style-rule-application(applied)
        . (level, member, taken, mismatch) = match-style-rule(made, applied.name, given)
        if level == invalid-type
            if !report-argument-types(member)
                decline(application)
            = false
        . named = taken
        . missed = mismatch
        if level != no-type
            levels += level
            members += member
            gates += U64.max
        else
            . (status, writes, last) = sheet-rules(made, applied.name, given, application, levels, members, gates, mismatch)
            if status == 1
                decline(application)
            if status != 0
                = false
            named = named || writes
            missed = last
        . (scoping, found, place-missed) = scope-rules(made, applied.name, given, element-scopes, scoped, missed)
        if scoping == 1
            decline(application)
        if scoping != 0
            = false
        if levels.length == 0 && scoped.length == 0 && (named || found)
            . place = if place-missed != U32.max then missed-value else application
                .. missed-value = tree.children[applied.args.start + place-missed]
            frame.diagnose(place, .stated, program.store-atom("Type mismatch"))
            = false
        if levels.length == 0 && scoped.length == 0 && !style-declared(applied.name)
            frame.diagnose(application, .stated, program.store-atom("No style rule is named \"${applied.name.text}\". Write one in a style sheet, or, where a library applies it for a theme to style, declare it there with an empty rule"))
            = false
        if several && given.length != 0 && (scoped.length != 0 || !variants-alike(levels, members))
            decline(application)
            = false
        .. several = levels.length + scoped.length > 1
        = true
decline(application)
= false

────────────────────
_ do variants-alike Bool
    - levels [TypeId]
    - members [DeclRef]

. wanted = rule-argument-types(members[0])
=? false if !wanted
for position in 1 .. < levels.length
    if family-root(levels[position]) != family-root(levels[0])
        = false
    . other = rule-argument-types(members[position])
    if !other || other.length != wanted.length
        = false
    for place in 0 .. < wanted.length
        if other[place] != wanted[place]
            = false
= true

────────────────────
_ do written-name SyntaxId
    - type-id SyntaxId
    - name Atom

` The type a markup element is written with where it is spelled as a style rule's name, at which
` the reference reports an error of the rule it applies by that name; or none.
do match? tree.nodes[written-base(tree, type-id)]
    | .node-type-identifier(written)
        if !written.is-declare && written.name == name
            = written-base(tree, type-id)
= 0

────────────────────
_ do apply-named U32
    - id SyntaxId
    - made TypeId
    - unit InstanceId
    - order U32
    - styled Bool
    - frames U32 = U32.max
    - cell U32 = U32.max
    - values U32 = U32.max
    - outer-cells U32 = U32.max

` Applies a style rule taking no values that a markup element matches by name, written by a
` class of its chain, a style sheet it sees or a rule within the `frames`, state cells and `values`
` given, typed by the
` instance `unit`, from an order, as `apply-style-rules` says, marked `shared` where the
` reference makes it a function (`shares-rule`): one with no rules around it, which matches no
` rule that has any as it applies its own. One that declares nothing makes the element a site
` all the same (`empty-shared`). Answers the order the next rule takes, or `U32.max`.
if unit == no-instance || !answers-alike(unit, made, id)
    decline(id)
    = U32.max
. active [InstanceId]
. applied [InstanceId]
. ungated [StyleWhen]
. first = facts.style-applications.length
. framing = framed
. next = apply-rule
    - id
    - made
    - unit
    - order
    - 0
    - U32.max
    - 0
    - ungated
    - active
    - applied
    - frames
    - cell
    - values
    - false
    - outer-cells
if next == U32.max
    = U32.max
if styled && frames == U32.max && framed == framing && shares-rule(applied, next - order)
    if next == order
        empty-shared = true
    facts.style-applications[first].shared = true
    revise-application(first as U32)
    facts.style-applications[first].made = made
    revise-application(first as U32)
    facts.style-applications[first].span = next - order
    revise-application(first as U32)
= next

────────────────────
+ do sheet-rules (U32, Bool, U32)
    - made TypeId
    - name Atom
    - given [TypeId]
    - at SyntaxId
    - matched [TypeId]
    - members [DeclRef]
    - gates [U64]
    - mismatch U32
    - own Bool = false
    - chained Bool = false

` The rules of the style sheets a markup element of a class sees that an application of a name
` answers, where no class of its chain does, as the reference's `resolveMatch` adds them: in
` each group, lowest first, the rule of each sheet that takes the values given most closely
` (`match-rules-of`), and of those the one that takes them most closely, two alike being the
` reference's error at `at`, or declined where `at` is none, and one whose types are written
` wrong reported where it is written (`report-argument-types`). Each group's applies, the lowest
` first. Answers 0, 1 where it is to be declined and 2 where it is reported; whether a sheet
` it looks at writes a rule of the name; and the place of the last value found not to convert.
` Where the sheets the markup sees are not known here (`sheets-known`), a name a rule of any
` sheet has is declined. With `own`, the sheets are those the class uses alone, as a rule the
` class writes chooses for the values it gives the rules it applies. With `chained`, they are
` those the class's chain uses and their variants, as the defaults of a class find the rules of
` its name (`apply-themed-defaults`).
if !sheet-rule-name(name)
    = (0, false, mismatch)
if !own && !chained && !sheets-known()
    = (1, false, mismatch)
. sheets [TypeId]
. levels [U32]
if own || chained
    add-sheet-groups(made, sheets, levels)
else
    visible-sheets(made, sheets, levels)
. named = false
. missed = mismatch
. top = if levels.length != 0 then levels[levels.length - 1] + 1 else 0u32
for group in 0 .. < top
    . best = no-type
    . best-kind = 0u32
    . tied = no-type
    . chosen-sheets [TypeId]
    . chosen-rules [DeclRef]
    . chosen-gates [U64]
    for place in 0 .. < sheets.length
        if levels[place] != group
            continue
        . family = family-members(sheets[place], own)
        if family.length > 64
            = (1, named, missed)
        . found-sheets [TypeId]
        . found-rules [DeclRef]
        . found-gates [U64]
        . (found, kind, writes, last) = family-rules(family, name, given, missed, found-sheets, found-rules, found-gates)
        if writes
            named = true
        missed = last
        if found && kind == U32.max
            = (if report-argument-types(found-rules[0]) then 2u32 else 1u32, named, missed)
        if !found
            continue
        if best == no-type || kind > best-kind
            best = sheets[place]
            best-kind = kind
            tied = no-type
            chosen-sheets = found-sheets
            chosen-rules = found-rules
            chosen-gates = found-gates
        else if kind == best-kind && tied == no-type
            tied = sheets[place]
    if tied != no-type
        if at == 0
            = (1, named, missed)
        . text = "Style rule \"${name.text}\" is ambiguous between visible style sheets ${type-short-name(types, best)} and ${type-short-name(types, tied)}"
        frame.diagnose(at, .stated, program.store-atom(text))
        facts.inset-diagnostic(0, name.text.length as U32)
        = (2, named, missed)
    for position in 0 .. < chosen-sheets.length
        matched += chosen-sheets[position]
        members += chosen-rules[position]
        gates += chosen-gates[position]
= (0, named, missed)

────────────────────
_ do family-members [TypeId]
    - root TypeId
    - alone Bool = false

. family [TypeId]
family += root
=? family if alone
list-derived-sheets()
for derived in facts.derived-sheets
    if family-root(derived) == root
        family += derived
= family

────────────────────
_ do family-rules (Bool, U32, Bool, U32)
    - family [TypeId]
    - name Atom
    - given [TypeId]
    - mismatch U32
    - sheets [TypeId]
    - rules [DeclRef]
    - gates [U64]

if family.length == 1
    . (held, rule, kind, writes, last) = match-rules-of(family[0], name, given, mismatch)
    if held
        sheets += family[0]
        rules += rule
        gates += U64.max
    = (held, kind, writes, last)
. found [Bool]
. chosen [DeclRef]
. kinds [U32]
. named = false
. missed = mismatch
for sheet in family
    . (held, rule, kind, writes, last) = match-rules-of(sheet, name, given, missed)
    named = named || writes
    missed = last
    if held && kind == U32.max
        rules += rule
        = (true, U32.max, named, missed)
    found += held
    chosen += rule
    kinds += kind
. picks [U32]
for position in 0 .. < family.length
    . pick = U32.max
    . level = family[position]
    while true
        . place = family.find(level)
        if place && found[place] && (pick == U32.max || kinds[place] > kinds[pick])
            pick = place as U32
        if level == family[0]
            break
        level = types.base-of(level) ?? family[0]
    picks += pick
. full = if family.length == 64 then U64.max else (1u64 /lshift/ family.length) - 1
. any = false
. best = 0u32
for place in 0 .. < family.length
    . mask = 0u64
    for position in 0 .. < picks.length
        if picks[position] == place as U32
            mask = mask /or/ (1u64 /lshift/ position)
    if mask == 0
        continue
    sheets += family[place]
    rules += chosen[place]
    gates += if mask == full then U64.max else mask
    if !any || kinds[place] > best
        best = kinds[place]
    any = true
= (any, best, named, missed)

────────────────────
_ do gate-applications Bool
    - first U32
    - sheet TypeId
    - mask U64
    - at SyntaxId

=? true if mask == U64.max
. family = sheet-index(family-root(sheet), module, at, at)
if family == U32.max || !demand-family-runtime()
    decline(at)
    = false
facts.family-gates += 1
for index in first .. < (facts.style-applications.length as U32)
    . held = facts.style-applications[index]
    if held.family != U32.max && held.family != family
        decline(at)
        = false
    facts.style-applications[index].family = family
    revise-application(index)
    facts.style-applications[index].members = if held.family == family then masked else mask
        .. masked = held.members /and/ mask
    revise-application(index)
= true

────────────────────
_ do apply-rule U32
    - id SyntaxId
    - made TypeId
    - unit InstanceId
    - order U32
    - written SyntaxId
    - outer U32
    - within SyntaxId
    - gated [StyleWhen]
    - active [InstanceId]
    - applied [InstanceId]
    - frames U32 = U32.max
    - cell U32 = U32.max
    - values U32 = U32.max
    - gives Bool = false
    - outer-cells U32 = U32.max

` Records a style rule applied to a markup element at the rule layer from an order, with the
` rules it applies itself, as the reference applies them: each name the rule writes after its
` own, then each the body of each of its `when`s does, is resolved for the element's class as
` a name the element writes is, and applied in turn, recorded after this one with this one as
` its `outer` and the `when` as its `within`. The values the rule gives one were typed and
` converted with the rule (`type-applied-values`), for the rule its own class chooses, which
` must be the one the element's class does. `gated` holds the `when`s the rule is applied
` under, the outermost first, which gate its declarations as `gate-when` says; a rule so gated
` that sets a property of its class is the reference's error. Answers the order the next rule
` takes, or `U32.max` where one is declined or reported. A rule that comes to apply itself
` again is the reference's error, at the application that would. `active` holds the rules
` being applied, the outermost first, and `applied` gathers each rule applied. A rule with a
` declaration whose value reads something tracked is given the constructor of the action of
` the style runtime that declares it again for the element's object, and one with a line that
` sets a property of its class again the function that makes that line's live action, chosen
` where the rule is applied, as `owner-action` chooses one for an attribute. A line of a rule a
` class writes whose value names a slot of a style sheet takes the slot the element sees
` (`bind-rule-slots`). The rules applied around the rule are `frames`; with the rule they are
` those around the rules it applies after its name, and around the rules written in it, which it
` brings into view after those (`bring-scopes`). A rule written in the body of a `when` is
