??
    chosen.decl != 0 && chosen.module == members[0].module && chosen.decl == members[0].decl

.. chosen = own-sheet-rule(class, name, given)

────────────────────
_ do own-sheet-rule DeclRef
    - level TypeId
    - name Atom
    - given [TypeId]

` The rule of style sheets a class or a style sheet that writes a style rule chooses for the
` values it gives a rule it applies, where no class of its chain answers the name: the one of
` the sheets the class uses that they choose, or for a sheet, which uses none, the one sheet of
` the program with a rule they choose (`program-sheet-rule`). None where there is no one rule.
. sheets [TypeId]
. members [DeclRef]
. gates [U64]
. (status, writes, last) = sheet-rules(level, name, given, 0, sheets, members, gates, U32.max, true)
if status != 0 || sheets.length > 1
    = DeclRef(0, 0)
if sheets.length == 1
    = members[0]
if types.intrinsic-of(level) != .style-sheet
    = DeclRef(0, 0)
= program-sheet-rule(name, given)

────────────────────
_ do program-sheet-rule DeclRef
    - name Atom
    - given [TypeId]

` The rule of a name that values given choose among the style sheets of the program that write
` one (`match-rules-of`), in modules the module being typed shares a case with, where only one
` sheet has such a rule, or none where no sheet or more than one does, or the rule takes a type
` not known here.
. sheets [DeclRef]
. position = facts.first-style-rule(name)
while position != U32.max
    . ref = facts.style-rules[position]
    position = facts.style-rule-nexts[position]
    if !program.shares-case(module, ref.module)
        continue
    do match? program.modules[ref.module].decls[ref.decl]
        | .decl-style-rule(rule)
            if rule.owner != 0 && is-sheet-decl(ref.module, rule.owner)
                . sheet = extended-sheet(owner-ref) ?? DeclRef(ref.module, rule.owner)
                    .. owner-ref = DeclRef(ref.module, rule.owner)
                . seen = false
                for held in sheets
                    if held.module == sheet.module && held.decl == sheet.decl
                        seen = true
                if !seen
                    sheets += sheet
. chosen = DeclRef(0, 0)
for sheet in sheets
    . level = types.class-with-args(sheet.module, sheet.decl, scratch.types.mark)
    if family-root(level) != level
        continue
    . (found, written, kind, named, last) = match-rules-of(level, name, given, U32.max)
    if found
        if chosen.decl != 0 || kind == U32.max
            = DeclRef(0, 0)
        chosen = written
= chosen

────────────────────
_ do apply-unit U32
    - id SyntaxId
    - made TypeId
    - unit InstanceId
    - order U32
    - gives SyntaxId
    - outer U32
    - within SyntaxId
    - gated [StyleWhen]
    - active [InstanceId]
    - applied [InstanceId]
    - owner ModuleId
    - nested SyntaxId
    - frames U32
    - cell U32 = U32.max
    - values U32 = U32.max
    - outer-cells U32 = U32.max

` Applies the rule a style rule applies at `nested` in a module, within the rules applied
` around it (`frames`), the state cells of the `when`s around it and the values of the rule around
` it that takes some, as `apply-rule` says, where the element's vocabulary answers its properties
` as the rule's does and it does not come to apply itself again, the reference's error.
if unit == no-instance || !answers-alike(unit, made, id)
    decline(id)
    = U32.max
. cycle = active.find(unit)
if cycle
    report-recursion(active, cycle, unit, owner, nested)
    = U32.max
= apply-rule
    - id
    - made
    - unit
    - order
    - gives
    - outer
    - within
    - gated
    - active
    - applied
    - frames
    - cell
    - values
    - false
    - outer-cells

