= true

────────────────────
_ do demand-object-pointer Bool

` The function of the style runtime that resolves the bits of a handle, typed once.
. runtime = facts.style-runtime
if runtime.object-pointer == no-instance
    . module-id = class-ref(types, types.type-row(.style)).module
    . mark = scratch.types.mark
    scratch.types.push(types.type-row(.int64))
    runtime.object-pointer = calls.demand-runtime-call
        - module-id
        - no-type
        - program.store-atom("style-object-pointer")
        - mark
    scratch.types.rewind(mark)
    facts.style-runtime = runtime
= runtime.object-pointer != no-instance

────────────────────
_ do flag-domain TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - domain String
    - below Bool
    - bare Bool
    - writes Bool

` A read or a write of the flag of a domain: the domain numbered as it is first named, and the
` function of the style runtime that reads or writes the flag of the subject cast to a
` `Pointer`, `style-node-domain-invalid` or `style-node-domain-write`, or their `-below`
` forms, a call that ends what is known of properties. A read gives a `Bool`. A bare one in a
` nested function is declined.
