` A class's style rules are told apart by name and by the type of what each takes: `• This`,
` the defaults rule, takes nothing, and no rule repeats one the class wrote before it. A style
` sheet has no defaults rule.
do match? tree.nodes[rule.syntax]
    | .node-rule-syntax(row)
        if rule.name.text == "This" && row.args.count != 0
            frame.diagnose
                - rule.syntax
                - .stated
                - program.store-atom("Style rule \"This\" must be parameterless")
            =
        . decls = program.modules[module].decls
        for earlier in 0 .. < index
            do match? decls[earlier]
                | .decl-style-rule(other)
                    if other.outer == 0 && namesake && repeats-rule(other.syntax, row.args)
                        frame.diagnose
                            - rule.syntax
                            - .stated
