            = false
        = same
= false

────────────────────
_ do same-signature (Bool, Bool)
    - left-tree AST
    - left RowRange'SyntaxId
    - right-tree AST
    - right RowRange'SyntaxId

` Whether two style rules take the same values, as the reference's `hasSameSignature` tells rules
` of one name apart: as many, each of a type written with the same name (`written-type-name`),
` the first that differs telling them apart; and whether that is known, false where a type it
` reaches is written in a way not named here.
if left.count != right.count
    = (false, true)
for offset in 0 .. < left.count
    . mine = written-type-name
        - left-tree
        - left-tree.rule-argument-type(left-tree.children[left.start + offset])
    . theirs = written-type-name
        - right-tree
        - right-tree.rule-argument-type(right-tree.children[right.start + offset])
    if !mine || !theirs
        = (false, false)
    if mine != theirs
        = (false, true)
= (true, true)

────────────────────
_ do choose-updater Bool
    - index U32
    - site SyntaxId
    - made TypeId

` Gives the application `index` of a rule with a line that sets a property of its class again
` as what its value read changes the function that makes that line's live action for an object
` of the class `made`, as `owner-action` chooses one for an attribute where the rule is
` applied, or marks those actions plain ones, and so for one with `live-values` whose rule sets a
` property with a value that reads them. Says whether that has a shape here.
. unit = facts.style-applications[index].unit
if !facts.updates-live(unit) && !(live-given && facts.updates-given(unit))
    = true
.. live-given = facts.style-applications[index].live-values
. rooted = owns-batch(made)
if owns-plain-actions(made) && !rooted
    facts.style-applications[index].plain-updates = true
else
    . maker = action-maker(site, made, rooted)
    if !maker
        = false
    facts.style-applications[index].updater = maker
    facts.style-applications[index].rooted = rooted
revise-application(index)
= true

────────────────────
+ do root-applications Bool
    - owner ModuleId
    - outlet SyntaxId
    - wanted TypeId

` Brings into view, in the function that builds what a line gives a slot, the rules written in
` rules that the rules the slot's outlet applies bring, as the reference's
` `markupSlotContentNodeWithRuleScopes` binds them: under state cells this function makes before
` it builds (at no element, `U32.max - 1`) and binds to what it built, read as of the slot's
` type. False where one is declined.
. written = program.modules[owner].tree
do match? written.nodes[outlet]
    | .node-slot-outlet(row)
        . none [Atom]
        . gathered [ScopeUse]
        if !gather-scopes(wanted, none, row.style-rule-applications, U32.max - 1, wanted, gathered, written)
            = false
        for use in gathered
            if use.scope.own != .scope-pending
                rule-scopes += use
        = true
= false

────────────────────
+ do applies-plainly Bool
    - element SyntaxId

` Whether a markup element other than a root `<This` is written in lines of markup alone, each
` an element of the body of the one around it, out to the markup of a class or to the body of
` the arm of a markup region the instance builds, where the reference opens no live action as it
` makes the element.
do match? tree.nodes[element]
    | .node-markup(row)
        if tree.names-this(row.type-id)
            = false
. arm = if frame.declaration.kind == .branch-arm-decl then frame.declaration.syntax else 0u32
. node = element
while true
    . holder = tree.holder-of(node)
    if holder == 0
        = false
    if holder == arm
        = true
    do match tree.nodes[holder]
        | .node-block
            node = holder
        | .node-markup(row)
            if node != row.body
                = false
            node = holder
        | .node-content-block
            = true
        ??
            = false

────────────────────
+ do names-unmodeled-style Bool
    - receiver TypeId
    - name Atom
    - site SyntaxId

` Whether a name no member answers is one the reference reads or writes on an object as a
` property of a style its class uses, or as the flag of a domain a `MarkupBatchFlush` reports,
` neither of which has a shape here yet.
if is-batch-flush(receiver)
    . (domain, _) = accessor-domain(name.text)
    = domain.length != 0
if types.intrinsic-of(receiver) == .interface
    = uses-styles(receiver)
if types.intrinsic-of(receiver) != .class
    = false
. styles [TypeId]
if !add-visible-styles(receiver, styles, site)
    = true
= style-answering(styles, name) != no-type

────────────────────
_ do uses-styles Bool
    - type TypeId

` Whether the declaration of a type names a style or a style sheet in a using.
. ref = class-ref(types, type)
. owner = program.modules[ref.module]
do match? owner.decls[ref.decl]
    | .decl-class(declared)
        for member in owner.member-pool[declared.members]
            if owner.decls[member] is .decl-using
                = true
= false

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ accessor-domain (String, Bool)
    - text String

` The domain whose flag a name of a style read names, `is-X-invalid` or `is-X-invalid-below`,
` and whether it is the flag below, as the reference's `styleDomainAccessor` matches it: no
` domain where the name is neither.
|? !text.starts-with("is-")
    ("", false)
|? text.ends-with("-invalid-below") && text.length > 17
    (text[3 .. < text.length - 14], true)
|? text.ends-with("-invalid") && text.length > 11
    (text[3 .. < text.length - 8], false)
??
    ("", false)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ slot-number U32
    - name String

` The number of a slot generated content fills, 0 to 3 for before, after, first-child and
` last-child, or `U32.max`.
|? name == "before"
    0
|? name == "after"
    1
|? name == "first-child"
    2
|? name == "last-child"
    3
??
    U32.max
